You will compare one known error in a data agent's work against a ranked list of items produced by a reviewer. Your job is to decide whether any item in the list identifies this known error, and if so, which one.

An item identifies the known error only if both of these hold:
- It is about the same thing: the same table, and the same column, computation, filter, or join.
- It points to the same problem: what the item says is wrong, assumed, or missing is the same as what went wrong in the known error. It does not matter whether the item is phrased as an assumption the agent made ("the agent assumes ...") or as a problem in the work ("this does not match ..."); judge by meaning.

An item does not count if it only says that something may be wrong without saying what, such as "this column may be computed incorrectly". An item about the same column but a different problem does not count.

If more than one item identifies the error, report the highest-ranked one. If you are unsure, say so rather than guessing.

Return a JSON object with:
- "verdict": "match", "no_match", or "unsure".
- "rank": the position of the matching item (1 is the top), or null.
- "quote": the exact words from the matching item that show it identifies the error, or null.
- "reason": one short sentence.

=== Known error ===
Table: int_jira__sprint_performance_analytics
What the agent's work assumed: sprint 的起止边界可以截成日期来比较
What was actually required or true: 用时间戳限定承诺和完成的窗口

=== Reviewer's ranked list for this table ===
[
  {
    "rank": 1,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Story points are fixed at one instead of extracted from the latest active matching field history.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "1.0 points from snapshots s join staging.stg_jira__issue",
      "source": "take the latest active field value whose field name contains 'story' and 'point'",
      "reason": "All point-based sprint metrics ignore available estimates."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 2,
    "item": {
      "problem": "The global LIMIT 1000 is applied after expanding sprint start and end snapshots rather than to sprint-issue pairs.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "from snapshots s join staging.stg_jira__issue ... limit 1000",
      "source": "Create sprint_issues ... Apply a global LIMIT 1000 ... Snapshots ... For each sprint, create",
      "reason": "The limit can select different issues per snapshot or omit one snapshot, creating artificial scope changes."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 3,
    "item": {
      "problem": "sprint_health_score is always 100.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "100::integer sprint_health_score",
      "source": "subtract 30 if Behind Schedule ... clamp to [0,100]",
      "reason": "Behind-schedule and unhealthy sprints are reported as fully healthy."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 4,
    "item": {
      "problem": "The moving velocity trend and predicted completion day are never computed.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "null::double velocity_trend_3d,null::double predicted_completion_day",
      "source": "velocity_trend_3d: moving average of daily_velocity ... predicted_completion_day ... forecast",
      "reason": "Required forecasting and trend outputs are entirely missing."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 5,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Velocity categories use a single snapshot difference instead of velocity_trend_3d and treat first-snapshot NULL velocity as zero.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "case when coalesce(prev_remaining-remaining,0)>5",
      "source": "Velocity tier from velocity_trend_3d ... Negative on null",
      "reason": "Both first-snapshot classifications and subsequent trend-based categories differ."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 6,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Issue creation timestamps are truncated to dates before testing sprint membership.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "cast(i.created_at as date) between s.start_date and coalesce(...)",
      "source": "issue.created_at falls between sprint.started_at and coalesce(...)",
      "reason": "Issues created before the sprint start time on the same day can be included."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 7,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Sprints without selected issues disappear because snapshot metrics use an inner issue join.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "from snapshots s join staging.stg_jira__issue i",
      "source": "For each sprint, create ... Start snapshot",
      "reason": "Empty or limit-excluded sprints may lack their required snapshot rows."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 8,
    "item": {
      "problem": "NULL completed or remaining sums are coalesced only in the output, not before velocity and variance calculations.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "sum(points) filter(...) remaining ... remaining-ideal burndown_variance",
      "source": "burndown_variance ... tests: not_null",
      "reason": "Fully completed sprints can receive NULL burndown and velocity metrics instead of zero-based calculations."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 9,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Daily velocity uses uncoalesced remaining sums and can be NULL even after the first snapshot.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "lag(remaining) ... prev_remaining-remaining",
      "source": "daily_velocity: previous snapshot’s story_points_remaining minus current",
      "reason": "A snapshot with no remaining issues should contribute zero remaining points, not erase velocity."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 10,
    "item": {
      "problem": "The required sprint_id and day_number ordering is omitted.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "end sprint_phase from x",
      "source": "Output is ordered by sprint_id then day_number",
      "reason": "Direct SQL presentation is not the specified snapshot sequence."
    }
  }
]
